    "On May 9th... She ate one per day."
    Does she eat the first one on May 9th? Yes, "She ate one per day" starting from the purchase.
    If she buys 40 eggs on May 9.
    May 9: Eat 1 (39 left)
    May 10: Eat 1 (38 left)
    ...
    May 31: Eat 1.
    Days in May: 9, 10, ..., 31. Count = $31 - 9 + 1 = 23$.
    Eggs left after May 31: $40 - 23 = 17$.
    June 1: Eat 1 (16 left)
    ...
    June 17: Eat 1 (0 left).
    So on June 17, she eats the last egg. She has 0 eggs. She has "run out".
    So "Today" = June 17.
    "Yesterday" = June 16.
    Still no option for June 16.

